          "formula": "Z_F=JZ_{F\\circ H},\\quad\\int_{T^{-1}B}e^{-F}dx=J\\int_Be^{-F\\circ H}dx.",
          "lean": "Measure.integral_comp_smul; integral_add_left_eq_self; integral_indicator"
        },
        {
          "title": "Cancel the Jacobian in the normalized law",
          "text": "Use map_apply on the measurable affine map and tilted_apply_eq_ofReal_integral on each measurable set. J!=0 cancels in the numerator/partition ratio. Mathlib totalizes improper integrals; this identity does not certify probability. The source consumer below derives positive integrability internally.",
          "formula": "\\frac{J\\int_Be^{-F\\circ H}}{JZ_{F\\circ H}}=\\frac{\\int_Be^{-F\\circ H}}{Z_{F\\circ H}}.",
          "lean": "Measure.map_apply; tilted_apply_eq_ofReal_integral'; integral_div; mul_div_mul_left"
        }
